+def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+    """
+    Light the seed frame and every frame reached through a chain of aligned one-cell ports.
+
+    Input structure:
+    - The background is black and contains several separated monochrome hollow rectangular frames.
+    - Each frame is one cell thick and has exactly one one-cell opening on one side.
+    - Exactly one frame contains a single yellow seed pixel in its interior; every other frame interior is empty.
+
+    Rule:
+    - The seed frame activates first, fills its interior yellow, and emits a yellow ray through its opening in that opening's outward direction.
+    - A ray paints every background cell it crosses; if it reaches another frame exactly at that frame's opening from the outside, that frame activates, fills yellow, and relays the signal forward along the same straight direction.
+    - If the ray would hit a wall before reaching a usable opening, it stops there; unactivated frames stay unchanged.
+
