   248	    Light the seed frame and relay the signal through every aligned port chain.
   249	
   250	    Input structure:
   251	    - The background is black and contains several separated monochrome hollow rectangular frames.
   252	    - Each frame is one cell thick and has exactly one one-cell opening on one side.
   253	    - Exactly one frame contains a single yellow seed pixel in its interior; every other frame interior is empty.
   254	
   255	    Rule:
   256	    - The seed frame activates first, fills its interior yellow, and emits a yellow ray through its visible opening in that opening's outward direction.
   257	    - A ray paints every background cell it crosses; if it reaches another frame exactly at that frame's opening from the outside, that frame activates, fills yellow, and the signal continues straight through the box to the opposite wall and onward in the same direction.
   258	    - If the ray would hit a wall before reaching a usable opening, it stops there; unactivated frames stay unchanged.
